  "worked_solution": "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{430}^{\u2218}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{\u2218}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{\u2218},{360}^{\u2218}).$\n\n- $-{430}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}=-{70}^{\u2218}$\n\n- $-{430}^{\u2218}+2\\cdot {360}^{\u2218}={290}^{\u2218}\\,\u2713$\n\nSo the angle ${290}^{\u2218}$ is coterminal with $-{430}^{\u2218}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944377/assets/dd07505860bd967a66911efca9f20f074798d3d1003776125bf186f7e359bd56.png)\n\nWe see that ${290}^{\u2218}$ lies in quadrant IV. Therefore, $-{430}^{\u2218}$ also lies in this quadrant.",
